        "short_description": "Placeholder for a national professional basketball league: 30 teams in two conferences of three divisions, 82-game regular season, play-in for seeds 7-10, four best-of-7 playoff rounds. Onboarding renames this and every Team N."
      },
      "lore": [
        {
          "title": "Structure",
          "display_index": 0,
          "content": "Conference A and Conference B, each with North, Central and South divisions of five teams. This file seeds no season, so no COMPETES_IN edges. When onboarding creates the first season it gives each team a COMPETES_IN edge with conference \"Conference A\" or \"Conference B\" and group the division alone (\"North\"), read from the team's tags (conference-a, division-north), which stay as the team's standing membership. Rename the competition, the teams (full name, short_name, abbreviation, city) and the conferences and divisions to what the owner's league uses; the tags can stay. Vocabulary: rule/sport_basketball; routine: rule/basketball_game_log."
        }
      ]
